# Project: LAED (laed.eu) — Secure Collaboration Platform

## What this is
A closed-loop collaboration platform for high-stakes confidential project work (M&A, legal, consulting). Security is the product; AI is an enhancement layer.

## Architecture
- Backend: FastAPI (Python), Poetry for package management
- Database: PostgreSQL 16 + pgvector, SQLAlchemy 2.0 + Alembic
- File storage: MinIO (S3-compatible, encrypted at rest)
- Vector search: pgvector (embeddings stored alongside relational data)
- Task queue: Celery + Redis
- LLM gateway: LiteLLM (routes to Ollama or paid providers)
- LLM: Ollama with Qwen 2.5 14B (on separate GPU server, open source default)
- STT: Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 (CPU, OpenAI-compatible API)
- Embeddings: nomic-embed-text via Ollama
- Frontend: Next.js PWA (mobile-first, no native app)
- Reverse proxy: Caddy with auto-TLS
- Container registry: Scaleway CR (rg.fr-par.scw.cloud/laed)
- Infrastructure: Scaleway (Paris) — GP1-XS base server + L4 GPU on-demand
- IaC: Terraform (infrastructure/terraform/)

## Infrastructure
- Base server: Scaleway GP1-XS, PAR-1, IP 51.15.207.5
- GPU server: Scaleway L4-1-24G (not yet provisioned, on-demand)
- Both on same Scaleway Private Network (172.16.0.0/22)
- Domain: laed.eu
- SSH key: ~/.id_ed25519-scaleway
- Tailscale VPN for admin access

## Key design principles
- All service communication via HTTP APIs with environment variable URLs
- Project isolation: each project gets own pgvector-scoped embeddings, MinIO bucket, chat rooms
- Open source models by default — LiteLLM gateway available for paid provider routing
- Docker Compose for orchestration, images pushed to Scaleway Container Registry
- No builds on server — all images built locally and pushed to registry

## Code conventions
- Python: Poetry for dependencies, type hints everywhere
- Always use async/await for database operations
- JWT auth with project-scoped claims
- API endpoints follow REST conventions at /api/...
